					<item>
				<guid>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-2036107#post-3765540</guid>
				<title>2935 &quot;O, Death&quot;</title>
				<link>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-2036107/scp-729-j#post-3765540</link>
				<description></description>
				<pubDate>Wed, 11 Apr 2018 04:23:05 +0000</pubDate>
				<wikidot:authorName>DrBad</wikidot:authorName>				<wikidot:authorUserId>2095057</wikidot:authorUserId>				<content:encoded>
					<![CDATA[
						 <p>SCP 2935</p> <p>Effects: 729-J was attached to a standard surveillance drone, which was sent into the SCP 2935 access point. SCP-729-J entered the 2935 reality without incident. Observations by the surveillance drone were consistent with previous explorations of SCP-2935.<br /> However, approximately 20 minutes into the flight, video equipment on the drone cut out without warning. Two minutes later, 729-J and the drone both came hurtling out of the SCP-2935 access point at roughly 140 miles per hour, as if they'd been propelled by an unknown force.</p> <p>Ten minutes after the drone and 729-J were returned to local reality, Foundation equipment detected a massive seismic disturbance in the area around the access point. Upon further investigation, this disturbance was determined to be coming from the SCP-2935 reality itself. A second drone was sent into the access point, only to find that the exit into the SCP-2935 reality had been blocked off by a wall of earth and granite, estimated to be at least several kilometers thick.</p> <p>Testing has been suspended indefinitely.</p> <p>Note from Dr. Curtis: <em>Way to go, you little freak. You creep out the death cave&#8230;</em></p> 
				 	]]>
				</content:encoded>							</item>
